# defk-specific Memcheck suppressions, on top of OTP's suppress.standard.
#
# Keep this file short: every entry hides a class of report from the runner.

# frame_tag_test.exs, "a frame with a foreign tag fails cleanly": the test
# stamps promoted frames with a wrong layout tag (__defk_corrupt_tags__), and
# defk_frame_dtor deliberately frees nothing for a foreign frame ("The leak
# (the binaries it owned) is accepted; a crash is not", priv/defk_runtime.h,
# defk-ls8). The abandoned owned table and its buffers are by design.
#
# Scoped to the one kernel library that test builds
# (Elixir.Defk.FrameTagTest.K-<key>.so), so the same leak anywhere else
# still fails the run. The indirect blocks (the buffers the table held) go
# with their definite parent.
{
   defk_frame_dtor_foreign_frame_owned_buffers
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:realloc
   fun:erts_sys_realloc
   fun:erts_realloc_fnf
   fun:enif_realloc
   obj:*Elixir.Defk.FrameTagTest.K-*.so
   ...
}
